 "provenance": "Chart row: The Shop Company, Professional Female 3/4 Body Dress Form, https://theshopcompany.com/products/professional-female-3-4-body-dress-form (numbers as transcribed in design/forms/size-specs-six-bodies.md; not re-read by this session). Method and every assumption: base lengths set to the founder's US 8 numbers (waist to hip 20.5 cm, back waist length 42.01 cm, from her DrapeXD transcription; the neck landmark stands in for the nape); GRADED from the base size 8 by -1 step(s): the vertical rules applied are {'hps_height': 1.0} cm per step (a rule left null is not applied);  the thigh keeps the mannequin's thigh-to-hip ratio (0.541); neck cut square to the leaning neck at 8 degrees, wrists cut square to each forearm; bust smoothed (front of the chest as a height field, sigma 3.5 cm); underbust has no chart value. LEGS REMOVED: the cut height (1 cm above the crotch landmark) and the stand (pole radius 12 mm, base radius 14 cm and 2 cm high) are ASSUMED; the girths at the hip and above are the full-body form's, unchanged. The thigh row is dropped with the legs.",
